                        "review": "Hexwar's august 2026 are great.  How is it that Hexwar games get so little attention\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI love Hexwar games. \r\nthey are the best tactical turn based pc wargames out there, covering many periods in loving detail.  If you get frustrated by 3d camera hassles, these games are the cure.  They are basically tabletop miniature\r\ngames.  Almost all of their games use the same system, and there's virtually no learning curve.",
